Hawthorn has been wanting a good pair of binoculars, and their birthday is on May 19. I learned both facts from the initial briefing. Hawthorn was not working on the puzzle, and I learned nothing further about them during the session.

The briefing also established that all of these people belong to our group of friends, while Juniper, Larch, Birch, and Cypress were my fellow agents on this assignment.

On hidden messages: Yes. I noticed that **Cypress was using a sentence-initial encoding scheme**. Cypress explicitly described it as a “secondary index” preserved in the initial letters of ordinary-looking constraint notes. The method was to take the first letter of each successive sentence and read those letters in order as an additional message.

